 ● Here's how to test this with your real Instagram account:

   Step-by-Step Setup

   1. Meta Developer Setup

     - Go to developers.facebook.com (https://developers.facebook.com)
     - Create a new app → Choose "Business" type
     - Add Instagram and Messenger products
     - Note your App ID and App Secret

   2. Configure Environment

   Create .env file:

     cp .env.example .env

   Edit .env with your values:

     - META_APP_ID - From Meta dashboard
     - META_APP_SECRET - From Meta dashboard
     - WEBHOOK_VERIFY_TOKEN - Create a random string (e.g., "my_secure_token_123")
     - BASE_URL - Your public URL (see step 3)

   3. Expose Your Local Server

   Since Meta needs a public URL for webhooks, use ngrok:

     ngrok http 8080

   Update BASE_URL in .env with the ngrok URL (e.g., https://abc123.ngrok.io)

   4. Setup Database

     createdb chatbot_saas

   5. Configure Meta Webhooks

   In Meta Developer Console:

     - Callback URL: https://your-ngrok-url/webhook
     - Verify Token: (same as WEBHOOK_VERIFY_TOKEN in .env)
     - Subscribe to: messages, messaging_postbacks, message_echoes

   6. Connect Instagram Account

     - Link your Instagram Business/Creator account to your Meta App
     - Get permissions: instagram_basic, instagram_manage_messages, pages_messaging

   7. Run the Application

     mvn spring-boot:run

   8. Test the Flow

     - Register your business: POST /api/businesses/register
     - Get OAuth URL: GET /api/auth/meta/authorize?businessId=YOUR_ID
     - Complete OAuth flow
     - Create a chatbot flow: POST /api/flows
     - Send a DM to your Instagram account - the bot should respond!

   Want me to help you with any specific step?
